<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">14 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 14 October, from 1066 to 1964.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/england" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1066 CE <span class="tih-ago">960 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William of Normandy defeats Harold II at Hastings</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a day-long battle near Hastings, Norman forces killed King Harold II and broke the English army. The conquest replaced England's ruling class and transformed its language, law and architecture.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1322 CE <span class="tih-ago">704 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert the Bruce routs Edward II at Old Byland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Scottish army under Robert the Bruce defeated English forces at Old Byland in Yorkshire, and Edward II narrowly escaped capture. The defeat pushed England towards the truce of 1323.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1586 CE <span class="tih-ago">440 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mary, Queen of Scots, goes on trial at Fotheringhay</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Mary was tried before a commission of English peers and officials at Fotheringhay Castle, accused of plotting Elizabeth I's death in the Babington Plot. Found guilty, she was beheaded in February 1587.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1890 CE <span class="tih-ago">136 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Dwight D. Eisenhower is born in Texas</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Dwight David Eisenhower was born in Denison, Texas. He commanded the Allied invasion of Europe in 1944 and served two terms as the 34th US president, warning on leaving office of the 'military-industrial complex'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dwight-d-eisenhower">Dwight D. Eisenhower</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1947 CE <span class="tih-ago">79 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Chuck Yeager flies faster than sound</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Captain Chuck Yeager piloted the rocket-powered Bell X-1 past Mach 1 high over the Mojave Desert. It was the first confirmed supersonic flight in level flight, opening the age of supersonic aviation.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1964 CE <span class="tih-ago">62 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet leaders oust Nikita Khrushchev</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Recalled from holiday, Nikita Khrushchev was forced out by the Communist Party's Central Committee. Leonid Brezhnev succeeded him as party leader and steered the Soviet Union into two decades of stability and stagnation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li></ol>
